From e59c3c77426946086e09ef44640df28fbe38b780 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 21:57:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] mm: shard file i_mmap trees by NUMA domain

Adapted from linux 7.0-rc1 patch to OLK-6.6.
- Added CONFIG_NUMA_DOMAIN_I_MMAP_SHARDS (defaults to n)
- Added per-NUMA i_mmap shard infrastructure with per-shard rwsems
- Modified rmap, unmap, pagewalk, khugepaged, memory-failure to iterate sharded trees
- Preserved fork-side file VMA batching and exit-side unlink batching by NUMA domain
- Keep DAX and hugetlb mappings on the legacy tree
- Added debugfs stats for i_mmap domain operations

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
