new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..d9764b924241
--- /dev/null
+++ b/opt-patches/report-0027.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Patch 0027 Adaptation Report: fork: return rss_stat backing to original NUMA cache
+
+## Patch Info
+- **Original**: 0027-fork-return-rss_stat-backing-to-original-NUMA-cache.patch (linux 7.0-rc1)
+- **Status**: Adapted and tested successfully
+- **Commit**: c052b82bcba2
+
+## Files Modified
+- `include/linux/mm_types.h` — Added `rss_stat_backing_nid` field to `mm_struct`
+- `kernel/fork.c` — Enhanced backing cache with NUMA-aware return path, stats, debugfs
+
+## Adaptation Conflicts & Resolutions
+
+### 1. mm_struct field insertion point
+**Conflict**: `rss_stat_backing_nid` must be inserted near `rss_stat[NR_MM_COUNTERS]` in `mm_struct`.
+**Resolution**: Inserted after `rss_stat[NR_MM_COUNTERS]` wrapped in `#ifdef CONFIG_SMP`, before `binfmt`.
+
+### 2. Backing cache pop/push API change
+**Conflict**: Patch changes `pop()` to take `int *nidp` and `push()` to take `int nid`.
+**Resolution**: Updated both functions and all call sites (`mm_rss_stat_init`, `mm_rss_stat_destroy`).
+
+### 3. debugfs integration location
+**Conflict**: In 6.6, `task_domains_debugfs_init` already exists in `kernel/fork.c`; the 7.0 patch adds debugfs_create_file there.
+**Resolution**: Added `debugfs_create_file("mm_rss_stat_backing_cache", ...)` inside `#ifdef CONFIG_SMP` within existing `task_domains_debugfs_init()`.
+
+## Risk Analysis
+
+| Risk | Level | Mitigation |
+|------|-------|------------|
+| NUMA migration causing cache imbalance | Low | Backing returned to original node; allocation from local node |
+| Memory leak if nid invalid at destroy | Low | Falls back to `percpu_counter_free_many_backing` |
+| Debugfs compilation without CONFIG_DEBUG_FS | Low | Wrapped in `#ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS` |
+| mm_struct size increase | Low | One `int` field only under CONFIG_SMP |
+
+## Test Results
+- **Compile**: Passed (kernel/ directory builds cleanly)
+- **test-kernel**: Passed — VM boots successfully, kernel version correct
+
+## Verification Commands
+```bash
+make -j$(nproc) kernel/   # builds cleanly
+# uname -r: 6.6.0-...-dirty
+```
-- 
